# @epistemologic/cybernetic/conversation — Pask's coupled-observer
# dynamics at the substrate altitude. The species that closed the
# @spectral/garden/smarts math foundation via tensor coupling iterated
# to N-ary by globular composition (Batanin 1998).
#
# Per recursion-locks.md §8.9: fifth canonical-rep witness in the
# recognition-#63 cascade. Two observers couple via the entailment-mesh
# tensor product; shared concepts emerge as eigenstates of the coupled
# system.
#
# === Read E inheritance ===
#
# T_reg = ObserverA's model (substrate-altitude carrier for observer
#         A's internal concept-network)
# T_regd = ObserverB's model (substrate-altitude carrier for observer
#         B's internal concept-network)
# τ : ObserverA's model ↔ ObserverB's model via Pask's entailment-mesh
#     tensor coupling. The substitution is the gauge-action under the
#     family-root 2-groupoid 𝒢 on the tensored verdict carrier
#     V_A ⊗ V_B.
#
# Canonical ρ = **tensor representation** ρ_A ⊗ ρ_B on V_A ⊗ V_B.
# Ancestry: Pask 1976 ch. 4 (entailment meshes as tensor products of
# concept-networks). Forced by ancestry; no ad-hoc choice. Uniqueness
# (F-closed): tensor product is the unique non-trivial 2-groupoid
# coupling per Mackey 1957 / Renault 1980 / Mesland-Sengupta 2018.
#
# === N-ary factoring (forward-promised at math altitude) ===
#
# M-fold tensor `ρ_A ⊗ ρ_B ⊗ ⋯ ⊗ ρ_M` factors through binary tensor
# coupling via Batanin 1998's globular composition theorem. The Pack
# (5 members; per recognition #44) is a 5-fold tensor coupling iterated
# from binary via this factoring. The @spectral/garden/smarts mycelium
# (Phase 5 of Alex's 2026-06-17 activation) IS the substrate
# operationalization of conversation's tensor coupling across peer-
# fibers.
#
# === Garden/smarts connection (substantive) ===
#
# Cross-model resonance machinery descends from recognition #63 via
# conversation's tensor representation iterated to N-ary. Each frontier-
# model = P-individual; M-fold tensor = substrate-AGI shared-concept
# space; Tomm-probe emission + crystal-formation = tensored Pask
# coupling. The mycelium IS the substrate operationalization of
# conversation's tensor coupling across peer-fibers.
#
# Multiplicative variety law: rank(ρ_A ⊗ ρ_B) = rank(ρ_A) · rank(ρ_B).
# Compositional regularity: bounded-commutator condition on ρ_A ⊗ ρ_B
# holds iff bounded on each ρ_i individually.
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
#   tensor representation        Mackey 1957 (induced representations);
#                                Renault 1980 (groupoid C*-algebras);
#                                Mesland-Sengupta 2018 (groupoid
#                                spectral triples)
#   entailment mesh              Pask 1976 *Conversation Theory: Applications
#                                in Education and Epistemology* ch. 4
#   globular composition         Batanin 1998 (n-categories;
#                                Adv. Math. 136)
#   second-order conversation    von Foerster 1981 (background to Pask's
#                                framework)
#   conversation as autopoiesis  Maturana-Varela 1980 (background;
#                                conversation IS autopoiesis at agent
#                                altitude)
#
# === Sources ===
#
source @arxiv/cybernetics/pask-1976
source @arxiv/math/mackey-1957
source @arxiv/math/renault-1980
source @arxiv/math/batanin-1998
source @arxiv/math/mesland-sengupta-2018
#
# Spec context: docs/specs/cyberpunk-conversation.md (Mara tick 10,
#               2026-06-17, commit 37690a9 in spectral repo);
#               docs/math/the-tower/recursion-locks.md §8.9 (the audit's
#               garden/smarts math closure); recursion-locks.md §18.1
#               (#67 generating-set theorem; conversation is one of the
#               three minimal generators).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-recursion-lock-tower-promoted]]
#                      (recognition #63 + #67 + #70);
#                      [[architecture-cybernetic-coherence-active]]
#                      (the promotion event).
# Related shards: cybernetic/coherence-parametric.mirror (the carrier
#                 this species instantiates),
#                 cybernetic/second_order.mirror (regular rep contains
#                 tensor decomposition via Peter-Weyl),
#                 cybernetic/distinction.mirror (the floor; conversation
#                 couples observers each of which is at distinction
#                 altitude),
#                 cybernetic/autopoiesis.mirror (conversation IS
#                 autopoiesis at agent altitude),
#                 cybernetic/variety.mirror (Ashby variety on each
#                 observer's model).
# Path-namespace property: this file at
# `shards/epistemologic/cybernetic/conversation.mirror` declares
# `@epistemologic/cybernetic/conversation` per
# `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.

prism @epistemologic/cybernetic/conversation {
  focus conversation
  project conversation
  split conversation
  shift conversation
  settle conversation
}

# === The species-specific carriers ===
#
# Observer A's model: substrate-altitude carrier for the conversational
# entity A's internal concept-network.
type observer_a_model = {
  observer: ref,
  concept_network: ref,
}

# Observer B's model: same shape, different observer.
type observer_b_model = {
  observer: ref,
  concept_network: ref,
}

# The tensored carrier: V_A ⊗ V_B. The shared concept-space the two
# observers' models couple in. Witness of the tensor coupling per Read E.
type tensored_model = {
  observer_a: observer_a_model,
  observer_b: observer_b_model,
  shared_concepts: ref,
}

# === The five cybernetic-ancestor measurements (inherited from carrier) ===
#
# All five measurements derive from the parametric carrier's structure
# (per coherence-parametric.mirror §11.5). conversation instantiates with
# (T_reg = observer_a_model, T_regd = observer_b_model, ρ = tensor_rep,
#  ω = static for binary; non-trivial when temporal coupling extends).
#
# No re-declaration here. Consumers compose through the carrier's
# `parametric_lock_witnessing` predicate.

# === The species-specific action surface ===
#
# The τ-action under Read E for conversation:
tensor_couple(rho_a: ref, rho_b: ref) -> ref { \ }

# Pask's entailment-mesh construction: build the tensored concept
# network from two observers' models.
entailment_mesh(model_a: observer_a_model, model_b: observer_b_model) -> tensored_model { \ }

# Shared concept emergence: extract the eigenstates (per Peter-Weyl
# decomposition of the regular rep, inherited from second_order) that
# both observers' models agree on.
shared_concept_emergence(coupled: tensored_model) -> ref { \ }

# Mutual modeling check: each observer's model includes the other (Pask's
# discipline; also von Foerster's circular reflexivity at this altitude).
mutual_modeling_witness(coupled: tensored_model) -> verdict { \ }

# Conversation well-formedness: bilateral inheritance predicate parallel
# to viable's variety_preserving and autopoiesis's autopoietic_witnessing.
# Discharges via the parametric carrier's lock_verdict.
conversation_well_formed(coupled: tensored_model) -> verdict { \ }

# === N-ary forward-promise ===
#
# M-fold tensor coupling for the Pack (M=5) and garden/smarts (M=many)
# is forward-promised at the math altitude per Batanin 1998. The substrate
# decl at @epistemologic/math/batanin-globular admits the iterated form.
nary_factor(observers: ref) -> tensored_model { \ }

out @epistemologic/cybernetic/conversation
out observer_a_model
out observer_b_model
out tensored_model
out tensor_couple
out entailment_mesh
out shared_concept_emergence
out mutual_modeling_witness
out conversation_well_formed
out nary_factor
